<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Thanesar State</h1><p class="st-meta">1763 CE – 1850 CE (approx.) · capital Thanesar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Sikh chiefship at the ancient pilgrimage town of Thanesar, annexed by the British when its line ended in 1850.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikhs</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirhind">Sirhind</a> in 1763–64, Sikh <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardar">sardars</a> divided the surrounding country, and a Sikh family established itself at Thanesar, the old town beside the sacred tanks of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurukshetra">Kurukshetra</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Thanesar came under British protection with the other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cis-sutlej-states">Cis-Sutlej states</a> in 1809. It was a small chiefship, and its history under the British is thinly recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The British took over Thanesar in 1850 when the ruling line failed, and it became part of a British district. The town is now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurukshetra">Kurukshetra</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haryana">Haryana</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="princely state, 1763 CE – 1850 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">princely state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Indian princely states</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:94.79%;width:1.73%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1763 CE – 1850 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thanesar</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sikhism; Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Punjabi, Haryanvi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Thanesar</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1806&amp;focus=thanesar-state" aria-label="Thanesar State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6676 1083 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Thanesar State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6996 1339L7364 1601"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6996 1339h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6996 1339h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Thanesar. <a href="/atlas?year=1806&amp;focus=thanesar-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

